<title>INDIA: India's RBI lowers cut-off at repo auction.</title>
<headline>India's RBI lowers cut-off at repo auction.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said it set a cut-off rate of 3.90 percent at a repo auction on Monday, down from 3.95 percent at the last auction.  </p>
<p>The RBI said it accepted four bids for 45 billion rupees out of six bids it received for 48 billion rupees.</p>
<p>The weighted average cut-off rate was 3.7950 percent.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
